diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 1a55755..2969b7c 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -6,7 +6,19 @@ In-memory inventory service. `api.handle(request)` maps a request
 
 ## Endpoints
 
-- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...]}`: every item, ordered by `id`.
+- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...], "next_cursor": <string or null>}`: one page
+  of items, ordered by `id`.
+  - `limit` (optional): integer from 1 to 100, default 20. Out of range or not
+    an integer → 400.
+  - `cursor` (optional): an opaque string taken from a previous response's
+    `next_cursor`. Pass it back unchanged to get the following page. Malformed
+    → 400.
+  - `next_cursor` is `null` on the last page. Without a cursor the first page
+    is returned.
+  - Errors return `{"error": "..."}`.
 - `GET /items/<id>` → the item, 404 when unknown, 400 when `id` is not a number.
 
+Example: `GET /items?limit=20` returns 20 items and a `next_cursor`; then
+`GET /items?limit=20&cursor=<next_cursor>` returns the next page.
+
 Run the tests with `python3 -m unittest`.
